welcome back keeping the community  healthy and fed that was the focus of a  special event in chinatown today  bianca holman explains safely giving a  hand to those in need the asian  community development council held a  family in focus kickoff event at the  chinatown plaza free flu vaccines  health insurance enrollment information  and boxes of food had cars  lined up down spring mountain road  organizers say with so many impacted by  the coven 19 pandemic  it's important to help keep people  afloat this was also a last-minute  effort to encourage nevadans to vote on  election day las vegas leaders like  congresswoman suzy lee stopped by to  support  normally we come here to this community  to celebrate  and seeing that now we are basically  supporting so many families who  have lost jobs have lost income because  of this pandemic but i think the thing  that gives me hope is the reason i love  our state and our city  is because we come together and help  each other out we are just as effective  as anyone else  and they don't really know how to  navigate where they can get support and  help  and that's reason why we're here today  not only to give out the food to the  family  but also to know what a service is  available the council will continue to  work with partnering organizations and  host future  family in focus events reporting in  chinatown bianca holman  8 news now
 

